WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
- I'm back with actress
and dog lover, Olivia Munn.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.900
Also joining us now is one
of America's top gearheads.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.540
He's hosted a whole slew of NASCAR shows.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.660
He's also covered the Kentucky Derby,

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.770
and the Olympics, as a
correspondent for NBC Sports.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.960
Now he's switching gears, get it,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.177
as host of the new smash hit game show,

00:00:18.177 --> 00:00:19.840
"Floor is Lava" on Netflix.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.990
Check it out.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.820
- [Rutledge] With Gerald's
basketball background,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.819
netting that last leap
should be no problem.

00:00:25.819 --> 00:00:29.195
(suspenseful music)

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.370
(liquid splashes)

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.320
Oh no.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.294
Houston, we've got a problem.

00:00:33.294 --> 00:00:35.317
- (screams) Ah, it's the lava, no!

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.854
(liquid bubbles)

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:43.913
- All right, y'all.

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:45.710
Well, let's bring
Rutledge Wood on in here.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.525
Hey, what's up, Rutledge, how ya doing?

00:00:47.525 --> 00:00:48.358
- Hi, guys.

00:00:48.358 --> 00:00:49.191
I'm great, how y'all doing?

00:00:49.191 --> 00:00:50.024
- Hey, Rutledge.

00:00:50.024 --> 00:00:51.460
- I've got Olivia Munn as well.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.600
I was like, I'm gonna keep her in,

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.000
'cause we both are into
games, and obviously--

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:55.927
- This is awesome.

00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:57.470
- "Floor is Lava" is hit.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.100
So, Rutledge, like your
show is ridiculous,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.100
but it's also insanely popular.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.000
So tell everybody how it works.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.140
- All right, so basically

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.100
we have a gigantic room
filled with magic lava.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.230
And you're probably wondering,
where do you get magic lava?

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.820
Craigslist, and I got a great deal

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.380
on about 80,000 gallons or so.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.900
And we have these insane kind of rooms.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.040
It might be a kitchen, it
might be a planetarium,

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.510
and you basically have to get
from one side to the other,

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.520
using your team.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.970
And whoever gets there the fastest,

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.370
with the most people, wins $10,000.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.040
So, I know you two love games.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.010
I feel like y'all would be naturals at it,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.187
but it's pretty hard.

00:01:35.187 --> 00:01:36.760
- I love games.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.090
It is probably pretty hard.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.062
Challenge accepted, Rutledge.

00:01:40.062 --> 00:01:41.980
(Rutledge laughs)

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.270
So wait, Olivia, did you
want to ask Rutledge anything

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.730
about the game, anything?

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:49.770
- I wanna know, how do
you guys come up with

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.510
the different obstacles all the time?

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.090
'Cause I feel like that's one
of the biggest challenges.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.140
How do you constantly
keep it new and fresh?

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.890
Kind of like Ninja Warrior-esque, right?

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:57.910
- Sure, yeah.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.060
Well, I mean, let's be honest.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.410
Let's give credit where credit's due.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.440
Without you, Olivia,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.140
I don't think stuff like this would exist.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.620
I mean, they could've
called it "Floor Olivia,"

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.530
but that's really besides the point.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.450
Okay so, that being said,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.050
it was this incredible
gal named Megan McGrath.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.777
She had this great idea that said,

00:02:14.777 --> 00:02:17.197
"Let's take this game that
we all played as kids,

00:02:17.197 --> 00:02:19.960
"and try to make it
fresh and fun and new."

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.360
Because like, Kelly's obviously in like

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.440
a world's hyper studio.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.990
But like Olivia, when
I see your living room,

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.250
I already think you're
kind of at an advantage.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.640
You've got chairs.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.640
I don't know if that wall
stuff could take my weight,

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.473
but it might take yours.

00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:38.020
Like, it's just a game that
anyone could play at home.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:38.970
So, it was trying to make

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.710
all these kind of secret things in there

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.677
and just make it fun for everybody.

00:02:42.677 --> 00:02:43.610
- Yeah.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.180
- Okay, well, Rutledge, Olivia
played this game as a kid.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.860
So, what house games
did you play as a kid?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.980
- Ooh, now keep in mind,
I grew up in Alabama.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.580
So, our games were a little more--

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.200
- I love the southern feel today, yes!

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.420
Okay, keep going.
- Right?

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.550
- Y'all know, our games are like who,

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.060
does anyone here own a ball?

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:00.893
You do?

00:03:00.893 --> 00:03:01.795
Let's play that game.

00:03:01.795 --> 00:03:03.890
(Kelly and Olivia laughing)

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.210
We played, my parents had a long hallway,

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.130
and we played dodge ball with,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:12.110
we would take like a bunch of
tube socks and ball them up.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:13.720
And we would like line
them up in this area.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.960
But, I don't know about y'all.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.730
There were some about being
a kid and being on carpet,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.410
and having things hurled
at you at a high velocity.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.940
I got hurt way more
often playing that game

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.930
than I should have, but
that's kinda the fun of it.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.650
- That reminds me of the game
that we'd play all the time,

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.720
as children who didn't have money,

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.000
which was, get in a blanket,

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.190
everybody into the blanket,
like all five kids,

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.590
the top of the stairs that are carpeted,

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.630
and then just make it down.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.577
- Yes, you slide down, like a sled!

00:03:42.577 --> 00:03:43.880
Yes.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.713
- We tried that.

00:03:44.713 --> 00:03:47.930
I tried that in the laundry
hamper, and it went pretty good,

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.310
but I was just big enough as a kid,

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.030
about a fourth stair down,
and I just sort of darted.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:53.863
- Toppled?

00:03:53.863 --> 00:03:54.696
- Yeah.

00:03:54.696 --> 00:03:56.410
But that's, you know, you live and learn.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.010
- That's awesome, that's awesome.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.610
Okay, so, Rutledge, I understand the game

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.220
has made you pretty popular
with your girls, right?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.053
- Yeah, it's fun.

00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:04.370
You know, I've got three daughters.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.520
And y'all know like there are
some projects that you do,

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.750
that your friends and family
are like really excited about.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.810
But for my daughter's
Elsie, Millie, and Hattie,

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.760
Elsie is 12, Millie is nine, Hattie's six,

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.380
they've never had something like this

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.570
where they could be that excited.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.530
And I knew it was a big
deal because Elsie, now 12,

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.250
beautiful young lady,
she's texting some friends.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.020
And so, this boy that I know
that kinda has a crush on her,

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.677
texted her, and the boy was like,

00:04:28.677 --> 00:04:30.239
"Hey, is that your dad

00:04:30.239 --> 00:04:32.540
"on that Netflix show, "'Floor is Lava?'"

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.980
And she was like, "Yeah."

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.870
And he said, "Cool, have
you seen all the shows?"

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.327
And she reads that text to me, like,

00:04:39.327 --> 00:04:41.537
"He asked if I saw the shows, Dad.

00:04:41.537 --> 00:04:43.583
"Of course I saw the shows!

00:04:44.437 --> 00:04:46.030
"How am I supposed to answer?"

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.940
And it was this incredible
moment, 'cause I thought like,

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.400
that's my girl, you bet.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.920
Did I see the shows?

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.210
It's my dad, of course I saw the show.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.043
So, it's really fun to--

00:04:55.043 --> 00:04:56.920
- My kids don't, I mean,

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.730
some kids don't watch
their parents' stuff,

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.350
they're like over it (laughs).

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.530
- Well, and let's be honest,

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.858
I've not been the hit
factory, Kelly, that you have.

00:05:04.858 --> 00:05:06.813
I'm sure after like, "Ah,
Mom's got another number one."

00:05:06.813 --> 00:05:10.600
- My kids are too young, they
don't care what I do (laughs).

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.433
- Well one day,

00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:13.230
like one day there's
gonna be this real thing

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.537
where they're like, "Oh my gosh.

00:05:14.537 --> 00:05:16.285
"Yeah, your mom's a hit maker.

00:05:16.285 --> 00:05:18.920
"She's like Midas touch, this is amazing."

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.450
So for right now, it's pretty cool

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:23.294
for the kids to have that
kind of thing, you know?

00:05:23.294 --> 00:05:26.045
- My dogs watch all of my things.

00:05:26.045 --> 00:05:26.878
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:26.878 --> 00:05:27.777
- Yes, huge fans.

00:05:27.777 --> 00:05:29.543
- I am a hit with them.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.420
All right, wait, Olivia,

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.100
so you're as competitive as I am, I hear.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.720
I'll bet, you know,

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.620
I might know a little bit more
about superheroes than you.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:40.490
I know you played superhero,
but I was just wondering

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.030
if you wanna play a
little game to find out.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.030
'Cause Rutledge kind of
challenged us a minute ago.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.250
I'm just saying.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.150
- I'm really bad,

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.400
I have like a horrible
memory with these things.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.000
- [Kelly] Okay.
- [Rutledge] That's perfect!

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.740
- I'm actually slightly terrified as well,

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.430
'cause while I do love the movies

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.620
and I love like growing up with them,

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.980
I don't know that I'm going to nail this.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.820
So watch us both epically
fail together (laughs).

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.140
Wait, Rutledge, will you
help us out by refereeing?

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.870
- Yeah, you know what, I
had a minute just then,

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.634
I just wrote a few questions.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.162
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:08.162 --> 00:06:09.500
- All right, y'all, I'm
back with Olivia Munn,

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.160
and "Floor is Lava" host, Rutledge Wood.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.970
We're going to play a special version

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.910
of Rutledge's game show right now.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.260
This is called, what is it called?

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.230
Let's show your sign.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.063
Show your sign.

00:06:19.063 --> 00:06:20.877
- It's called, "Oh-Lav-ia."

00:06:20.877 --> 00:06:22.853
- "Oh-Lav-ia," get it?

00:06:22.853 --> 00:06:25.580
(upbeat rock music)

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:26.860
All right, here's how it works.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.530
Rutledge will read each
of us a trivia question,

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.460
one at a time.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.300
If we get it right, we get a point.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.770
But, if Olivia or I get it wrong,

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:38.210
we have to take a shot of lava, or a sip.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:42.040
AKA hot sauce that we have
here at our Zoom desks.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.940
And whoever gets the most points wins.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.330
So, and in honor of Olivia and me,

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:48.880
because I love superheroes too,

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.420
all the trivia questions
are superhero theme.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.253
So, here we go.

00:06:52.253 --> 00:06:53.242
Are you guys ready?

00:06:53.242 --> 00:06:55.070
- (exhales) This feels so official.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:58.570
Like that was absolute
official game show read.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.910
That was so impressive.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:00.743
- Rutledge, I'm in it.

00:07:00.743 --> 00:07:02.310
Okay.
- [Rutledge] In it to win it.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.910
- This is "Oh-Lav-ia," go.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.180
- Here we go.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.013
- Okay.

00:07:06.013 --> 00:07:08.020
- Question one, this one's for Olivia,

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.780
which film started off

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.657
the current Marvel superhero universe?

00:07:13.657 --> 00:07:14.853
- "Iron Man."

00:07:14.853 --> 00:07:15.686
(bell dings)

00:07:15.686 --> 00:07:16.560
- Oh, that's correct.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.400
She's on the board.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.480
- Hey, Kelly, I'm just
gonna drink my water,

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:21.794
not the hot sauce.

00:07:21.794 --> 00:07:23.100
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.530
- Oh, show off, okay.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.410
- Rubbing it in, I love Olivia Munn!

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:27.243
Okay.

00:07:27.243 --> 00:07:28.160
- Little bit of a flex there.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:28.993
Here we go.

00:07:28.993 --> 00:07:33.630
Question two, Kelly, what
weapon does Thor carry?

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:35.900
- Oh, a hammer (scoffs).

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.733
You know what?

00:07:36.733 --> 00:07:39.322
Gonna take a little bit of my milk, Oliva.

00:07:39.322 --> 00:07:41.350
- Oh, wow.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.120
- I'm lactose intolerant.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.770
- Me too, mine's almond (laughs).

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:47.696
(Rutledge laughs)

00:07:47.696 --> 00:07:48.863
- Mine's oat.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.600
- Yeah, I wanna say, y'all
better get right with oatly,

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.433
that stuff's amazing.

00:07:52.433 --> 00:07:54.416
Here we go, question three.

00:07:54.416 --> 00:07:56.640
Olivia, "Oh-Lav-ia,"

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.450
how many actors have played the role

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.443
of Peter Parker slash Spiderman,
in the live action films?

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:09.883
- Tobey Maguire, Andrew
Garfield, the new British kid.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.997
He's British, right?

00:08:11.997 --> 00:08:14.285
- Is that really important right now?

00:08:14.285 --> 00:08:17.650
(both girls laugh)

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.553
- You don't know how my mind works.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.650
- Let's just assume
then, yes, he's British.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:26.100
- And there was, well
those are the first three,

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.740
but then there's more after that.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.430
I'm gonna say, live
actions, TV and everything,

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:31.263
it's gotta to be more.

00:08:31.263 --> 00:08:33.560
Let's say, it's gonna be
like 10, or 15, or 20,

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:36.410
or 10, or 12.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.272
- You are totally taking
this hot sauce, chick.

00:08:38.272 --> 00:08:39.105
(buzzer buzzes)

00:08:39.105 --> 00:08:40.283
- Three, drink up.

00:08:40.283 --> 00:08:41.520
- [Olivia] It was three?
- [Rutledge] It was three.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.800
Yes, you had it, then
you doubted yourself.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.230
- The thing I didn't know
he was tricking you on,

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.669
if that that new one,
the animated one counted.

00:08:48.669 --> 00:08:50.949
- Well, I didn't know if he meant back in

00:08:50.949 --> 00:08:55.310
like the olden days,
was there another one?

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:56.560
- I would have given you four,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:00.620
but 15 is just, it's not,
that's not four's neighbor.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:03.830
- First of all, I love your
vat of hot sauce (laughs).

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.150
- By the way, this came
from you, Kelly Clarkson.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:09.190
I know, okay, well I love
that we sent you the pandemic,

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.301
the Costco version of hot sauce.

00:09:12.301 --> 00:09:13.860
We wanted you to not run out in the next--

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.020
- We got this, we got this.

00:09:16.469 --> 00:09:18.560
You guys sent me shot glasses.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.393
- Drink up (laughs).

00:09:19.393 --> 00:09:21.286
- Oh, wow, boy, just--

00:09:21.286 --> 00:09:22.119
- It comes out really slow.

00:09:22.119 --> 00:09:22.952
Is this enough?

00:09:22.952 --> 00:09:23.785
- You can literally sip,

00:09:23.785 --> 00:09:25.860
'cause I literally have
to sing after this.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.700
I can't shoot this.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.533
